sers/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102028#pullrequestreview-2574194473","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102028","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102028#pullrequestreview-2574194473"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102028"}},"submitted_at":"2025-01-26T10:25:48Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2618388511,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6cEXAf","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nHowever, doing this kind of breaks the point of using a mesh-based texture in the first place. It is no longer a vector-based output (MeshTexture drawing a true 3D mesh into a 2D space), but a projection of a ViewportTexture. In that sense, it ends up just being a helper for something you can already do with a ViewportTexture.\r\n\r\nSetups like these are no longer possible, where you use existing 3D meshes to create true vector-based drawings without needing to use Line2D or Polygon2D:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7da41915-0597-46a1-9371-70b951ce8cc9)\r\n\r\n(This also benefits from 2D MSAA when enabled, as evidenced in the above screenshot.)\r\n\r\nOn top of that, using viewports has a performance impact that is not present when drawing meshes directly to 2D (unless the mesh is *very* complex, which is generally not the case in 2D).\r\n\r\nI would prefer we fix the flexibility issues that MeshInstance has (such as the lack of offset and scale properties and the bounding box issues) without changing fundamentally how it works.\r\n\r\nIf you want to use MeshTexture in 3D, you can essentially achieve the same thing with a MeshInstance3D with a custom shader that flattens vertices.[^1] This means no custom viewport is needed and the drawing is still vector-based in nature (and benefits from 3D MSAA).\r\n\r\n[^1]: A quick solution that doesn't need a custom shader is to scale the mesh by a very low value like `0.001` on one of the axes.\r\n\r\nRemember that for viewport-based drawing, [drawable textures](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7379) could be a superior alternative too.\r\n\r\n> In addition, when using GradientTexture2D as base_texture, change the property of gradient won't update texture in editor, because GradientTexture2D calls emit_changed signal before its texture updates. NoiseTexture2D is OK.\r\n\r\nI can confirm this issue.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102028#pullrequestreview-2618388511","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102028","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102028#pullrequestreview-2618388511"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102028"}},"submitted_at":"2025-02-14T17:14:05Z","commit_id":"7b1cfe0efdad97f4e7647a76e0a03663fbb357b5"}]